course: dictionary
lesson: 15370
title: Sown and the seeds of meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sown is the past form of the verb sow, which means to plant seeds in the ground so they can grow. You may also see sow written as sowed in some older books, but sown is the form used after has, have or had.
explain: «The farmer has sown wheat in the field.» The words has sown tell you the seeds are already in the ground. Try the swap: «The farmer has planted wheat in the field.» It still makes sense, so sown means planted, here as seeds.
explain: Sown can also mean spread with something. «The hill was sown with wild flowers» does not mean the flowers were planted one by one. It means the hill was covered with them, like a field sown with seeds. The clue is the word with after sown.
fact: Sow is a verb meaning to plant seeds, and sown is its past participle.
fact: «Sown» means planted as seeds, as in «The farmer has sown wheat.»
fact: «Sown with» means spread or covered with something, as in «a field sown with seeds».
fact: «You reap what you sow» is a saying that means what you do comes back to you.
fact: Farmers often sow seeds in spring, when the weather warms up and the seeds can grow.
exercise: «The farmer has sown wheat in the field.» What does sown mean here? | *Planted as seeds | Cut down with a scythe | Eaten by birds | Watered and washed
exercise: The saying «You reap what you sow» means? | *What you do comes back to you | Farmers must work hard all day | Wheat grows fastest in spring | Seeds should always be eaten
exercise: «The meadow was sown with daisies.» What was the meadow sown with? | *Daisies | Snow | Puddles | Stones
test: A farmer has sown 3 fields. Each field has 2 bags of seed. How many bags has she sown in total? | 23 | *6 | 5 | 8
test: Which word completes the sentence: The seeds have been ___ in the soil? | sow | sowing | *sown | sew
exam: What does sown mean in «The hill was sown with wild flowers»? | Painted red | Cut down | Climbed up | *Spread with, or planted with
